🏦 Business Case: Retail Banking Customer & Loan Performance Analytics
Company

Nexus Bank India (fictional)

Nexus Bank is a mid-sized retail bank operating across major Indian cities. It offers personal, home, auto, education, business and gold loans along with savings/current accounts and digital banking services.

The bank's leadership team has noticed that:

Loan applications are growing, but approval rates vary considerably.
Some loan products have significantly higher delinquency.
Branch performance varies across regions.
Digital channels are growing, but management doesn't know whether they attract better customers.
Some customer segments use multiple banking products while others remain low-engagement.
Management wants better visibility into credit-risk and loan-portfolio performance.

The CEO has asked the Analytics team to investigate.

🎯 Your Role

You are a:

Business/Data Analyst – Retail Banking Analytics

You report to:

Head of Retail Banking

Your stakeholders are:

Chief Executive Officer
Head of Retail Banking
Chief Risk Officer
Head of Sales
Regional Managers
Branch Managers
Finance Team

Your job isn't simply to create charts.

Your job is to answer:

"What is happening in our retail banking business, why is it happening, and what should management investigate or change?"

📋 Stakeholder Requirement
Message from Head of Retail Banking

Subject: Retail Banking Customer & Loan Performance Review

We need a comprehensive analysis of our retail banking customer and loan portfolio.

Senior management currently receives separate reports from branches, sales and risk teams. These reports don't provide a unified view of customer behavior, loan performance and branch/channel performance.

I want the Analytics team to create a single analytical view of our retail banking business.

Specifically, we need to understand:

How our customer base is distributed across segments and geographies.
How loan applications are performing.
Which loan products and customer segments are driving the portfolio.
Where approval and rejection rates are highest.
Where delinquency and default risk appears concentrated.
How branches and acquisition channels are performing.
How customer transaction behavior differs across segments.
Whether digital acquisition channels are producing meaningful customer activity.

The final analysis should identify the most important business issues and provide actionable recommendations for management.

